# Clay code

Studio and a generated app follow one standard. The full text is `templates/web-app/docs/code.md`.

- JavaScript with JSDoc. No in-code TypeScript syntax. Zod at every boundary. Change the contract before the handler.
- Noun paths. Verbs are HTTP methods. Writes send `Idempotency-Key`. Errors are `{ code, message, requestId }`. Status changes are declared transitions.
- React 19 (`react` and `react-dom` ^19.3.1). Function components. `ref` is a prop. A form submits through its `action`. `useActionState` from `react` holds a submit result and pending state. The automatic JSX runtime stays on. `eslint-plugin-react-hooks` recommended rules stay on.
- `node scripts/stack-versions.js` warns when a direct production dependency is behind the npm `latest` tag. Repeat that warning.
- Pure functions. Do not mutate shared data. Compare with `===`. A component stays at or under 50 lines.
- No customer, payment, HR, or secret data in prompts, logs, or seed data.
- `/plan` before implementation. Docs change in the same change as the behavior.
